<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch bond yield survey - March.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch bond yield survey - March.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reuters continues its monthly survey of bank economists' forecasts of levels for key Dutch interest rates in one month's time. Tabulated results follow:</p>
<p>		     3-MTH   5-YR   10-YR   LONG    5-YR   10-YR</p>
<p>							     SPREAD  SPREAD</p>
<p>							     (to Bunds, bp)</p>
<p>CURRENT	    3.20    4.87   5.78    6.47     -3     -11</p>
<p>ABN AMRO</p>
<p>HOARE GOVETT     3.15    4.85   5.80    6.50     -4     -10</p>
<p>GENERALE BANK    3.20    4.83   5.75    6.45     -5     -13</p>
<p>ING BARINGS	3.15    4.80   5.70    6.40     -5     -12</p>
<p>IRIS		 3.20    5.10   5.90    6.60     -7	-5</p>
<p>MEESPIERSON	3.20    4.90   5.85    6.50     -5	-9</p>
<p>RABOBANK</p>
<p>INTERNATIONAL    3.25    4.88   5.68    6.43     -3	-7</p>
<p>NIB SECURITIES   2.95    4.62   5.62    6.20     -7     -17</p>
<p>NOTES - The relevant benchmark bonds are the 8.25 pct Feb 15,</p>
<p>2002, 5.75 pct Feb 15, 2007 and 7.50 pct Jan 5, 2023 Dutch state</p>
<p>loans (DSLs) and the 8.00 pct Jan 21, 2002 and 6.00 pct Jan 4,</p>
<p>2007 Bunds.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000, fax 31 20 504 5040</p>
